[statement]
Solaris's extended header (typeflag `X`), carrying a path as a pax header
would. GNU tar, bsdtar and Python apply it to the next member, and Go reads
it as a regular file, so the readers disagree on the members. ferrotape
refuses it.

[archive]
header name=PaxHeader typeflag=X
records path=renamed
header name=victim
data "hello\n"
end

[verdict]
all: refused SolarisExtendedHeader at 0

[gnu-tar 1.35]
member listed=- path=renamed size=6 mode=0o644 data="hello\n"
exit 0

[bsdtar 3.8.11]
member listed=- path=renamed size=6 mode=0o644
exit 0

[python 3.12.3]
member type=0 path=renamed size=6 mode=0o644 mtime=0 uid=0 gid=0 uname=root gname=root data="hello\n"
ok

[go 1.27.0]
member type=X path=PaxHeader size=16 mode=0o644 mtime=0 uid=0 gid=0 uname=root gname=root data="16 path=renamed\n"
member type=0 path=victim size=6 mode=0o644 mtime=0 uid=0 gid=0 uname=root gname=root data="hello\n"
ok
